#@title 4. 云端 API（供本地提示词工具连接）
import hashlib, html, json, os, re, secrets, socket, subprocess, sys, time, urllib.request
from pathlib import Path
from IPython.display import HTML, Markdown, display

GATEWAY_SOURCE = '"""Authenticated, streaming ComfyUI gateway. Bind locally; tunnel port 8190 only."""\nimport argparse\nimport asyncio\nimport hmac\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.parse import parse_qs, quote, unquote\n\nimport aiohttp\nfrom aiohttp import web\nfrom multidict import CIMultiDict\nfrom yarl import URL\n\nCOOKIE = "moss_session"\nHOP = {"connection", "keep-alive", "proxy-authenticate", "proxy-authorization",\n       "te", "trailer", "transfer-encoding", "upgrade"}\nSESSION = web.AppKey("client", aiohttp.ClientSession)\nNO_STORE = {"Cache-Control": "no-store"}\nLOGIN = """<!doctype html><html lang="zh-CN"><meta charset="utf-8">\n<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">\n<title>MOSS ComfyUI Login</title><body>\n<h1>MOSS ComfyUI</h1><form method="post" action="/_moss/login">\n<label>API key <input type="password" name="api_key" maxlength="512"\nrequired autocomplete="off"></label><button type="submit">Login</button>\n</form></body></html>"""\n\n\ndef normalize_userdata(raw_path, method):\n    """Repair only Comfy userdata filenames decoded into paths by Colab\'s proxy."""\n    path, separator, query = raw_path.partition("?")\n    for prefix in ("/userdata/", "/api/userdata/"):\n        if not path.startswith(prefix):\n            continue\n        suffix = path[len(prefix):]\n        parts = suffix.split("/move/", 1) if method == "POST" and "/move/" in suffix else [suffix]\n        if any("/" in part for part in parts):\n            encoded = [quote(unquote(part), safe="") for part in parts]\n            path = prefix + "/move/".join(encoded)\n        break\n    return path + separator + query\n\n\ndef same_origin(request):\n    origin = request.headers.get("Origin")\n    if not origin:\n        return True\n    try:\n        parsed = URL(origin)\n        return parsed.scheme in ("http", "https") and parsed.raw_authority.lower() == request.host.lower()\n    except ValueError:\n        return False\n\n\ndef filtered_headers(headers, request=False):\n    blocked = HOP | {part.strip().lower() for part in headers.get("Connection", "").split(",")}\n    if request:\n        blocked |= {"host", "authorization", "cookie", "origin", "referer"}\n    else:\n        blocked |= {"set-cookie"}\n    return CIMultiDict((key, value) for key, value in headers.items()\n                        if key.lower() not in blocked\n                        and not key.lower().startswith("access-control-"))\n\n\ndef equal(value, expected):\n    try:\n        return hmac.compare_digest(value.encode("utf-8"), expected.encode("utf-8"))\n    except UnicodeError:\n        return False\n\n\ndef error(status, message):\n    return web.json_response({"error": message}, status=status, headers=NO_STORE)\n\n\nPUBLIC_MODEL_FIELDS = {"id", "display_name", "family", "version", "assets", "checkpoint",\n                       "text_encoder", "vae", "source_url", "notes"}\n\n\ndef asset_parts(value):\n    """Accept only canonical, portable paths relative to the configured model root."""\n    if (not isinstance(value, str) or not value\n            or any(character in value for character in "\\\\:<>|?*\\x00")\n            or any(ord(character) < 32 for character in value)):\n        raise ValueError("Invalid catalog asset path")\n    parts = value.split("/")\n    if any(part in ("", ".", "..") or part.endswith((".", " ")) for part in parts):\n        raise ValueError("Invalid catalog asset path")\n    return parts\n\n\ndef asset_ready(root, name, expected_size):\n    """Use metadata only; preparation verifies checksums before files become usable."""\n    current = root\n    parts = asset_parts(name)\n    for index in range(len(parts) + 1):\n        if index:\n            current = current / parts[index - 1]\n        try:\n            metadata = current.lstat()\n        except (FileNotFoundError, NotADirectoryError):\n            return False\n        # Windows junctions/reparse points also redirect paths without being symlinks.\n        if (stat.S_ISLNK(metadata.st_mode)\n                or getattr(metadata, "st_file_attributes", 0) & getattr(stat, "FILE_ATTRIBUTE_REPARSE_POINT", 0)):\n            raise ValueError("Catalog assets must not traverse links")\n        if index < len(parts) and not stat.S_ISDIR(metadata.st_mode):\n            return False\n    return stat.S_ISREG(metadata.st_mode) and metadata.st_size == expected_size\n\n\ndef load_model_catalog(catalog_path, model_root):\n    if not catalog_path or not model_root:\n        raise ValueError("Model catalog is not configured")\n    with Path(catalog_path).open(encoding="utf-8") as source:\n        catalog = json.load(source)\n    if (not isinstance(catalog, dict) or type(catalog.get("schema_version")) is not int\n            or catalog["schema_version"] != 1\n            or not isinstance(catalog.get("models"), list)\n            or not isinstance(catalog.get("files"), list)):\n        raise ValueError("Invalid model catalog")\n    files = {}\n    for item in catalog["files"]:\n        if not isinstance(item, dict):\n            raise ValueError("Invalid catalog file")\n        name = item.get("path")\n        asset_parts(name)\n        size = item.get("size_bytes")\n        if name in files or type(size) is not int or size < 0:\n            raise ValueError("Invalid catalog file")\n        files[name] = size\n    selected = catalog.get("selected_for_startup", [])\n    if not isinstance(selected, list) or any(not isinstance(item, str) for item in selected):\n        raise ValueError("Invalid startup selection")\n    models, identifiers = [], set()\n    for model in catalog["models"]:\n        if not isinstance(model, dict):\n            raise ValueError("Invalid catalog model")\n        identifier = model.get("id")\n        if not isinstance(identifier, str) or not identifier or identifier in identifiers:\n            raise ValueError("Invalid catalog model ID")\n        identifiers.add(identifier)\n        assets = model.get("assets")\n        if not isinstance(assets, list) or not assets:\n            raise ValueError("Invalid model assets")\n        for name in assets:\n            asset_parts(name)\n            if name not in files:\n                raise ValueError("Unknown model asset")\n        for field in ("checkpoint", "text_encoder", "vae"):\n            if field in model and (not isinstance(model[field], str) or model[field] not in assets):\n                raise ValueError("Unknown model asset alias")\n        public = {key: value for key, value in model.items() if key in PUBLIC_MODEL_FIELDS}\n        if any(not isinstance(value, str) for key, value in public.items() if key != "assets"):\n            raise ValueError("Invalid model metadata")\n        if "source_url" in public:\n            source = URL(public["source_url"])\n            if source.scheme != "https" or not source.host or source.user is not None:\n                raise ValueError("Invalid model source URL")\n        defaults = model.get("suggested_defaults")\n        if defaults is not None:\n            if not isinstance(defaults, dict):\n                raise ValueError("Invalid model defaults")\n            public["suggested_defaults"] = {\n                key: value for key, value in defaults.items()\n                if key in {"steps", "cfg", "sampler", "scheduler"}}\n            if any(not isinstance(value, (int, float, str)) for value in public["suggested_defaults"].values()):\n                raise ValueError("Invalid model defaults")\n        models.append(public)\n    if any(identifier not in identifiers for identifier in selected):\n        raise ValueError("Unknown startup model")\n    root = Path(model_root).absolute()\n    readiness = {name: asset_ready(root, name, files[name])\n                 for name in {name for model in models for name in model["assets"]}}\n    for model in models:\n        model["ready"] = all(readiness[name] for name in model["assets"])\n        model["selected_for_startup"] = model["id"] in selected\n    return {"protocol_version": 1, "models": models}\n\n\n"""Content-addressed LoRA routes, embedded verbatim by update_notebook.py.\n\nOnly the configured runtime and Drive model roots are writable. This module\ndoes not fetch remote resources and relies on the enclosing gateway\'s auth.\n"""\nimport asyncio\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport tempfile\n\nfrom aiohttp import web\n\n\nLORA_MAX_BYTES = 4 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024\nLORA_CHUNK_BYTES = 1024 * 1024\nLORA_TRANSFER_BYTES = 8 * 1024 * 1024\n\n\nclass LoraAssetConflict(ValueError):\n    pass\n\n\nclass LoraAssetInvalid(ValueError):\n    pass\n\n\nclass LoraGatewayStore:\n    def __init__(self, model_root, catalog_path):\n        self.runtime_root = Path(model_root).absolute() if model_root else None\n        self.drive_root = Path(catalog_path).absolute().parent / \'models\' if catalog_path else None\n        self.locks = {}\n\n    def lock(self, sha256):\n        return self.locks.setdefault(sha256, asyncio.Lock())\n\n    def path(self, root, sha256, *, create=False):\n        if root is None:\n            raise LoraAssetConflict(\'LoRA storage is not configured\')\n        # Do not follow a symlink at any level, including configured roots.\n        for ancestor in reversed((root, *root.parents)):\n            if ancestor.is_symlink() or (hasattr(ancestor, \'is_junction\') and ancestor.is_junction()):\n                raise LoraAssetConflict(\'LoRA storage cannot contain symlinks\')\n        directory = root / \'loras\' / \'anima_library\'\n        for part in (root, root / \'loras\', directory):\n            if part.is_symlink() or (part.exists() and not part.is_dir()):\n                raise LoraAssetConflict(\'LoRA storage must use regular directories\')\n            if create:\n                part.mkdir(exist_ok=True, parents=True)\n        target = directory / (sha256 + \'.safetensors\')\n        if target.is_symlink() or (target.exists() and not target.is_file()):\n            raise LoraAssetConflict(\'LoRA asset must be a regular file\')\n        return target\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def verified_size(path, sha256):\n        try:\n            fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | getattr(os, \'O_NOFOLLOW\', 0) | getattr(os, \'O_BINARY\', 0))\n        except FileNotFoundError:\n            return 0\n        except OSError as exc:\n            raise LoraAssetConflict(\'Cannot safely read LoRA asset\') from exc\n        with os.fdopen(fd, \'rb\') as stream:\n            before = os.fstat(stream.fileno())\n            if not stat.S_ISREG(before.st_mode) or not 0 < before.st_size <= LORA_MAX_BYTES:\n                return 0\n            digest = hashlib.sha256()\n            while chunk := stream.read(LORA_CHUNK_BYTES):\n                digest.update(chunk)\n            after = os.fstat(stream.fileno())\n            if ((before.st_size, before.st_mtime_ns, before.st_ctime_ns)\n                    != (after.st_size, after.st_mtime_ns, after.st_ctime_ns)):\n                return 0\n            return before.st_size if digest.hexdigest() == sha256 else 0\n\n    def status(self, sha256):\n        runtime = self.verified_size(self.path(self.runtime_root, sha256), sha256)\n        cached = self.verified_size(self.path(self.drive_root, sha256), sha256)\n        result = {\'sha256\': sha256, \'size_bytes\': runtime or cached,\n                \'cached\': bool(cached), \'installed\': bool(runtime),\n                \'file_name\': \'anima_library/\' + sha256 + \'.safetensors\'}\n        if not runtime and not cached:\n            state = self.partial_state(sha256)\n            if state:\n                result.update(upload_offset=state[\'offset\'], upload_total_bytes=state[\'total\'])\n        return result\n\n    def partial_paths(self, sha256, *, create=False):\n        target = self.path(self.drive_root, sha256, create=create)\n        paths = (target.parent / (\'.\' + sha256 + \'.upload.part\'),\n                 target.parent / (\'.\' + sha256 + \'.upload.json\'))\n        for path in paths:\n            if path.is_symlink() or (path.exists() and not path.is_file()):\n                raise LoraAssetConflict(\'LoRA partial must be a regular file\')\n        return paths\n\n    def partial_state(self, sha256):\n        partial, metadata = self.partial_paths(sha256)\n        if not metadata.exists():\n            return None\n        try:\n            if metadata.stat().st_size > 4096:\n                raise ValueError()\n            state = json.loads(metadata.read_text(encoding=\'utf-8\'))\n            if (not isinstance(state, dict) or type(state.get(\'offset\')) is not int\n                    or type(state.get(\'total\')) is not int\n                    or not 0 <= state[\'offset\'] < state[\'total\'] <= LORA_MAX_BYTES\n                    or not partial.exists() or partial.stat().st_size < state[\'offset\']):\n                raise ValueError()\n            return state\n        except (ValueError, OSError, UnicodeError) as exc:\n            raise LoraAssetConflict(\'LoRA upload metadata is invalid\') from exc\n\n    def commit_offset(self, sha256, offset, total):\n        _, metadata = self.partial_paths(sha256, create=True)\n        fd, name = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=\'.\' + sha256 + \'-\', suffix=\'.json.part\', dir=metadata.parent)\n        temporary = Path(name)\n        try:\n            with os.fdopen(fd, \'w\', encoding=\'utf-8\') as output:\n                json.dump({\'offset\': offset, \'total\': total}, output)\n                output.flush()\n                os.fsync(output.fileno())\n            self.partial_paths(sha256)\n            os.replace(temporary, metadata)\n        finally:\n            temporary.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n\n    def clear_partial(self, sha256):\n        for path in self.partial_paths(sha256):\n            path.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n\n    async def upload_range(self, request, sha256):\n        match = re.fullmatch(r\'bytes (\\d+)-(\\d+)/(\\d+)\', request.headers.get(\'Content-Range\', \'\'))\n        if match is None:\n            raise LoraAssetInvalid(\'Invalid Content-Range\')\n        start, end, total = map(int, match.groups())\n        length = end - start + 1\n        if (not 0 <= start <= end < total <= LORA_MAX_BYTES\n                or not 0 < length <= LORA_TRANSFER_BYTES or request.content_length != length\n                or request.headers.get(\'Content-Encoding\', \'identity\').lower() != \'identity\'):\n            raise LoraAssetInvalid(\'Invalid range size or encoding\')\n        partial, _ = self.partial_paths(sha256, create=True)\n        state = self.partial_state(sha256)\n        if state is not None and (state[\'total\'] != total or state[\'offset\'] != start):\n            raise LoraAssetConflict(\'Query the committed upload offset before retrying\')\n        if state is None:\n            if start:\n                raise LoraAssetConflict(\'Upload must start at offset zero\')\n            with partial.open(\'wb\'):\n                pass\n            await asyncio.to_thread(self.commit_offset, sha256, 0, total)\n        # A disconnected chunk may have written a suffix without committing it.\n        # Truncate to the last atomic metadata offset before accepting a retry.\n        received = 0\n        with partial.open(\'r+b\') as output:\n            output.truncate(start)\n            output.seek(start)\n            async for chunk in request.content.iter_chunked(LORA_CHUNK_BYTES):\n                received += len(chunk)\n                if received > length:\n                    raise LoraAssetInvalid(\'Chunk is larger than its range\')\n                await asyncio.to_thread(output.write, chunk)\n            if received != length:\n                raise LoraAssetInvalid(\'Chunk is incomplete\')\n            await asyncio.to_thread(output.flush)\n            await asyncio.to_thread(os.fsync, output.fileno())\n        if end + 1 < total:\n            await asyncio.to_thread(self.commit_offset, sha256, end + 1, total)\n            return\n        if await asyncio.to_thread(self.verified_size, partial, sha256) != total:\n            await asyncio.to_thread(self.clear_partial, sha256)\n            raise LoraAssetInvalid(\'Final upload SHA-256 does not match\')\n        target = self.path(self.drive_root, sha256)\n        os.replace(partial, target)\n        await asyncio.to_thread(self.clear_partial, sha256)\n        await asyncio.to_thread(self.install, sha256)\n\n    def install(self, sha256):\n        source = self.path(self.drive_root, sha256)\n        if not self.verified_size(source, sha256):\n            raise LoraAssetConflict(\'Verified Drive cache is not available\')\n        target = self.path(self.runtime_root, sha256, create=True)\n        fd, name = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=\'.\' + sha256 + \'-\', suffix=\'.part\', dir=target.parent)\n        temporary = Path(name)\n        try:\n            digest, size = hashlib.sha256(), 0\n            with os.fdopen(fd, \'wb\') as output, source.open(\'rb\') as stream:\n                while chunk := stream.read(LORA_CHUNK_BYTES):\n                    size += len(chunk)\n                    if size > LORA_MAX_BYTES:\n                        raise LoraAssetInvalid(\'LoRA asset exceeds the size limit\')\n                    digest.update(chunk)\n                    output.write(chunk)\n                output.flush()\n                os.fsync(output.fileno())\n            if not size or digest.hexdigest() != sha256:\n                raise LoraAssetInvalid(\'Drive asset changed during restoration\')\n            self.path(self.runtime_root, sha256)\n            os.replace(temporary, target)\n        finally:\n            temporary.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n\n    async def upload(self, request, sha256):\n        length = request.content_length\n        if length is not None and not 0 < length <= LORA_MAX_BYTES:\n            raise LoraAssetInvalid(\'LoRA content length is outside the size limit\')\n        if request.headers.get(\'Content-Encoding\', \'identity\').lower() != \'identity\':\n            raise LoraAssetInvalid(\'LoRA upload must use unencoded raw bytes\')\n        target = self.path(self.drive_root, sha256, create=True)\n        fd, name = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=\'.\' + sha256 + \'-\', suffix=\'.part\', dir=target.parent)\n        temporary = Path(name)\n        try:\n            digest, size = hashlib.sha256(), 0\n            with os.fdopen(fd, \'wb\') as output:\n                async for chunk in request.content.iter_chunked(LORA_CHUNK_BYTES):\n                    size += len(chunk)\n                    if size > LORA_MAX_BYTES or (length is not None and size > length):\n                        raise LoraAssetInvalid(\'LoRA upload length exceeds the limit\')\n                    digest.update(chunk)\n                    # Drive writes run off the event loop so status/auth remains responsive.\n                    await asyncio.to_thread(output.write, chunk)\n                if not size or (length is not None and size != length) or digest.hexdigest() != sha256:\n                    raise LoraAssetInvalid(\'LoRA upload size or SHA-256 does not match\')\n                await asyncio.to_thread(output.flush)\n                await asyncio.to_thread(os.fsync, output.fileno())\n            self.path(self.drive_root, sha256)\n            os.replace(temporary, target)\n            await asyncio.to_thread(self.clear_partial, sha256)\n            await asyncio.to_thread(self.install, sha256)\n        finally:\n            temporary.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n\n\ndef register_lora_routes(app, model_root, catalog_path):\n    store = LoraGatewayStore(model_root, catalog_path)\n\n    async def lora_asset(request):\n        sha256 = request.match_info.get(\'sha256\', \'\')\n        if not re.fullmatch(r\'[0-9a-f]{64}\', sha256):\n            return web.json_response({\'error\': \'A lowercase SHA-256 asset ID is required\'}, status=422)\n        restore = request.path.endswith(\'/restore\')\n        allowed = (\'POST\',) if restore else (\'GET\', \'PUT\')\n        if request.method not in allowed:\n            return web.json_response({\'error\': \'Unsupported LoRA method\'}, status=405,\n                                     headers={\'Allow\': \', \'.join(allowed)})\n        try:\n            async with store.lock(sha256):\n                status = await asyncio.to_thread(store.status, sha256)\n                if restore and not status[\'installed\']:\n                    await asyncio.to_thread(store.install, sha256)\n                elif request.method == \'PUT\':\n                    # Even when cached, validate bytes supplied to PUT. Ordinary\n                    # cache reuse uses GET/restore and sends no local bytes.\n                    if request.headers.get(\'Content-Range\'):\n                        await store.upload_range(request, sha256)\n                    else:\n                        await store.upload(request, sha256)\n                status = await asyncio.to_thread(store.status, sha256)\n                return web.json_response(status, headers={\'Cache-Control\': \'no-store\'})\n        except LoraAssetConflict:\n            return web.json_response({\'error\': \'LoRA cache is unavailable or has an unsafe path\'}, status=409)\n        except (LoraAssetInvalid, asyncio.IncompleteReadError, ConnectionError):\n            return web.json_response({\'error\': \'LoRA upload is incomplete or failed verification\'}, status=422)\n        except OSError:\n            return web.json_response({\'error\': \'LoRA storage operation failed; retry safely\'}, status=503)\n\n    app.router.add_route(\'*\', \'/_moss/loras/{sha256}\', lora_asset)\n    app.router.add_route(\'*\', \'/_moss/loras/{sha256}/restore\', lora_asset)\n    app.router.add_route(\'*\', \'/_moss/loras/{tail:.*}\', lora_asset)\n\n\ndef create_app(upstream="http://127.0.0.1:8188", api_key=None, browser_session=None,\n               catalog_path=None, model_root=None, runtime_id=None):\n    api_key = api_key if api_key is not None else os.environ.get("MOSS_API_KEY", "")\n    browser_session = browser_session if browser_session is not None else os.environ.get("MOSS_BROWSER_SESSION", "")\n    if not (24 <= len(api_key) <= 512 and 24 <= len(browser_session) <= 512):\n        raise ValueError("MOSS_API_KEY and MOSS_BROWSER_SESSION must each contain 24-512 characters")\n    if equal(api_key, browser_session):\n        raise ValueError("MOSS_BROWSER_SESSION must differ from MOSS_API_KEY")\n    target = URL(upstream)\n    if (target.scheme not in ("http", "https") or target.host not in ("127.0.0.1", "::1", "localhost")\n            or target.user is not None or target.path not in ("", "/") or target.query_string or target.fragment):\n        raise ValueError("Upstream must be an HTTP loopback origin, for example http://127.0.0.1:8188")\n    base = str(target.origin())\n    catalog_path = catalog_path if catalog_path is not None else os.environ.get("MOSS_MODEL_CATALOG", "")\n    model_root = model_root if model_root is not None else os.environ.get("MOSS_MODEL_ROOT", "")\n\n    runtime_id = runtime_id if runtime_id is not None else os.environ.get("MOSS_RUNTIME_ID", "")\n    if (not isinstance(runtime_id, str) or len(runtime_id) > 128\n            or any(char not in "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789_.-" for char in runtime_id)):\n        raise ValueError("Invalid runtime identity")\n\n    @web.middleware\n    async def authenticate(request, handler):\n        if request.path == "/_moss/login" and request.method in ("GET", "POST"):\n            return await handler(request)\n        header = request.headers.get("Authorization", "")\n        if header.startswith("Bearer ") and equal(header[7:], api_key):\n            return await handler(request)\n        if equal(request.cookies.get(COOKIE, ""), browser_session):\n            if not same_origin(request):\n                return error(403, "Cross-origin browser requests are not allowed")\n            return await handler(request)\n        return error(401, "API key required; use Authorization: Bearer or /_moss/login")\n\n    async def login(request):\n        if request.method == "GET":\n            return web.Response(text=LOGIN, content_type="text/html",\n                                headers={**NO_STORE, "Content-Security-Policy":\n                                         "default-src \'none\'; form-action \'self\'; frame-ancestors \'none\'; base-uri \'none\'"})\n        if not same_origin(request):\n            return error(403, "Cross-origin login is not allowed")\n        try:\n            body = await request.content.readexactly(4097)\n        except asyncio.IncompleteReadError as exc:\n            body = exc.partial\n        if len(body) > 4096:\n            return error(413, "Login body is too large")\n        if request.content_type != "application/x-www-form-urlencoded":\n            return error(415, "Submit the login form")\n        try:\n            submitted = parse_qs(body.decode("utf-8"), max_num_fields=4).get("api_key", [""])[0]\n        except (ValueError, UnicodeError):\n            return error(400, "Invalid login form")\n        if len(submitted) > 512 or not equal(submitted, api_key):\n            return error(401, "Invalid API key")\n        response = web.HTTPSeeOther("/", headers=NO_STORE)\n        response.set_cookie(COOKIE, browser_session, secure=True, httponly=True,\n                            samesite="Lax", path="/")\n        raise response\n\n    async def info(request):\n        payload = {"service": "moss-comfyui-gateway", "version": 1,\n                   "auth": "bearer-or-browser-session", "upstream": "ComfyUI"}\n        if runtime_id:\n            payload["runtime_id"] = runtime_id\n        return web.json_response(payload, headers=NO_STORE)\n\n    async def models(request):\n        if request.method != "GET":\n            response = error(405, "Model catalog supports GET only")\n            response.headers["Allow"] = "GET"\n            return response\n        try:\n            payload = await asyncio.to_thread(load_model_catalog, catalog_path, model_root)\n        except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError, UnicodeError):\n            return error(503, "Model catalog is unavailable")\n        return web.json_response(payload, headers=NO_STORE)\n\n    async def websocket(request, url, headers):\n        socket = web.WebSocketResponse(autoclose=False, max_msg_size=0)\n        if not socket.can_prepare(request).ok:\n            return error(400, "Invalid WebSocket handshake")\n        try:\n            remote = await request.app[SESSION].ws_connect(\n                url, headers=headers, autoclose=False, max_msg_size=0)\n        except (aiohttp.ClientError, asyncio.TimeoutError):\n            return error(502, "ComfyUI WebSocket is unavailable")\n        async def relay(source, destination):\n            while True:\n                message = await source.receive()\n                if message.type == aiohttp.WSMsgType.TEXT:\n                    await destination.send_str(message.data)\n                elif message.type == aiohttp.WSMsgType.BINARY:\n                    await destination.send_bytes(message.data)\n                else:\n                    code = source.close_code or 1000\n                    code = code if code not in (1005, 1006, 1015) else 1011\n                    return code, (message.extra or "").encode("utf-8")\n\n        tasks = []\n        code, reason = 1000, b""\n        try:\n            await socket.prepare(request)\n            tasks = [asyncio.create_task(relay(socket, remote)), asyncio.create_task(relay(remote, socket))]\n            done, _ = await asyncio.wait(tasks, return_when=asyncio.FIRST_COMPLETED)\n            code, reason = next(iter(done)).result()\n        except (aiohttp.ClientError, ConnectionError, RuntimeError):\n            code = 1011\n        finally:\n            for task in tasks:\n                task.cancel()\n            await asyncio.gather(*tasks, return_exceptions=True)\n            await remote.close(code=code, message=reason)\n            if socket.prepared:\n                await socket.close(code=code, message=reason)\n        return socket\n\n    async def proxy(request):\n        # encoded=True preserves model names and query values containing %2F.\n        url = URL(base + normalize_userdata(request.raw_path, request.method), encoded=True)\n        headers = filtered_headers(request.headers, request=True)\n        if request.headers.get("Upgrade", "").lower() == "websocket":\n            for key in list(headers):\n                if key.lower().startswith("sec-websocket-"):\n                    del headers[key]\n            return await websocket(request, url, headers)\n        response = None\n        try:\n            async with request.app[SESSION].request(\n                    request.method, url, headers=headers, allow_redirects=False,\n                    data=request.content.iter_chunked(65536) if request.can_read_body else None,\n                    skip_auto_headers={"Content-Type", "Accept-Encoding"}) as remote:\n                response = web.StreamResponse(status=remote.status, reason=remote.reason,\n                                              headers=filtered_headers(remote.headers))\n                await response.prepare(request)\n                async for chunk in remote.content.iter_chunked(65536):\n                    await response.write(chunk)\n                await response.write_eof()\n                return response\n        except (aiohttp.ClientError, asyncio.TimeoutError, ConnectionError):\n            if response is not None and response.prepared:\n                response.force_close()\n                return response\n            return error(502, "ComfyUI is unavailable")\n\n    async def lifecycle(app):\n        async def reject_redirect(session, context, params):\n            raise aiohttp.ClientConnectionError("Upstream redirects are disabled")\n        trace = aiohttp.TraceConfig()\n        trace.on_request_redirect.append(reject_redirect)\n        timeout = aiohttp.ClientTimeout(total=None, connect=30, sock_connect=30)\n        app[SESSION] = aiohttp.ClientSession(\n            timeout=timeout, auto_decompress=False, cookie_jar=aiohttp.DummyCookieJar(),\n            trace_configs=[trace])\n        yield\n        await app[SESSION].close()\n\n    app = web.Application(middlewares=[authenticate], handler_args={"auto_decompress": False})\n    app.cleanup_ctx.append(lifecycle)\n    app.router.add_route("GET", "/_moss/login", login)\n    app.router.add_route("POST", "/_moss/login", login)\n    app.router.add_route("GET", "/_moss/info", info)\n    app.router.add_route("*", "/_moss/models", models)\n    register_lora_routes(app, model_root, catalog_path)\n    app.router.add_route("*", "/{tail:.*}", proxy)\n    return app\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument("--port", type=int, default=8190)\n    parser.add_argument("--upstream", default="http://127.0.0.1:8188")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    if not 1 <= args.port <= 65535:\n        parser.error("--port must be between 1 and 65535")\n    try:\n        app = create_app(args.upstream)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        parser.error(str(exc))\n    web.run_app(app, host="127.0.0.1", port=args.port, access_log=None, print=None)\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n\n'
API_README = "# MOSS / ComfyUI 云端接口\n\n本文件描述云端连接协议；本地提示词工具和配套工作流由另一台电脑单独适配。\n\n## 启动和连接\n\n在 MOSS_ComfyUI_OneClick.ipynb 点击“全部运行”。最后一个单元格将创建临时 HTTPS 入口，并显示 API 地址及访问密钥。\n\n- API 根地址：最后一格显示的 https://随机名称.trycloudflare.com，不添加 /api/v1。\n- 请求头：Authorization: Bearer <本次访问密钥>。\n- 请求和返回格式：ComfyUI 原生 API。这里不是 OpenAI 的 images/generations 接口。\n- 网页登录入口：API 根地址后添加 /_moss/login。浏览器先输入访问密钥登录，使用 HttpOnly 会话 Cookie。\n- 运行时回收后，地址与密钥失效；同一运行时重复运行复用已有进程和密钥。\n- 密钥不硬编码进源码，不存入本文件；连接配置在临时文件 /content/moss_connection.json，可从 Colab 文件面板下载。\n- 笔记本关闭“保存代码输出”，避免把本次密钥长期写进笔记本。不要分享密钥或连接配置。\n- ComfyUI 和认证代理只监听运行时本机回环地址，公网隧道只转发认证代理。\n\n## 接口\n\n所有下列接口都需要认证：\n\n| 方法 | 路径 | 作用 |\n|---|---|---|\n| GET | /_moss/info | 网关协议及服务信息 |\n| GET | /_moss/models | 已接入模型、家族、建议参数、当前本地是否就绪 |\n| GET | /system_stats | ComfyUI 版本和设备状态 |\n| GET | /object_info | 节点定义、可选模型文件和输入格式 |\n| GET | /queue | 当前运行和排队任务 |\n| POST | /prompt | 提交 ComfyUI API 格式工作流，返回 prompt_id |\n| GET | /history/{prompt_id} | 查询指定任务结果 |\n| GET | /view?filename=...&subfolder=...&type=output | 下载图片，参数取自历史记录的 images 项 |\n| POST | /upload/image | multipart/form-data 上传素材 |\n| POST | /queue | 删除指定排队任务，body 为 {\"delete\":[\"prompt_id\"]} |\n| GET | /ws?clientId=... | 可选的 WebSocket 事件；原生程序可改用历史轮询 |\n\nPOST /prompt 的 body 形状为：\n\n```json\n{\"prompt\":{\"节点ID\":{\"class_type\":\"节点类型\",\"inputs\":{}}},\"client_id\":\"本机客户端随机ID\"}\n```\n\n必须提交 ComfyUI 的 API 格式 JSON（节点含 class_type 和 inputs），不能把编辑器 nodes/links JSON 直接发给 /prompt。\n\n## 接入时的最小顺序\n\n1. 用 /_moss/info 和 /system_stats 测试连接；未带密钥应得到 401。\n2. 用 /object_info 核对节点和模型文件名。\n3. 将本地构建的 MOSS API 工作流发送到 /prompt，保存返回的 prompt_id。\n4. 轮询 /history/{prompt_id}，确认 status 成功或检查执行错误。\n5. 对每个 images 条目调用 /view，保存图片。\n\nPOST /prompt 超时后不要盲目自动重试，以免重复提交。先检查队列/历史并向用户报告不确定状态。HTTP 401 表示缺少或错误密钥；连接失败通常是运行时已停止、临时地址失效或隧道尚未就绪。\n\n示例（只检查连接，不提交出图）：\n\n```python\nimport os, requests\nbase = os.environ['MOSS_API_URL'].rstrip('/')\nheaders = {'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + os.environ['MOSS_API_KEY']}\nresponse = requests.get(base + '/system_stats', headers=headers, timeout=(10, 30))\nresponse.raise_for_status()\nprint(response.json()['system'])\n```\n\n## 范围与文件\n\n权重从 /content/moss_models 加载。成品图保存在 Drive 的 ComfyUI_Colab/output；上传素材保存在 input；用户设置和已保存工作流在 user。\n\n当前官方模型文件名：\n\n- moss_image_sft_int8_convrot.safetensors\n- qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq.safetensors\n- flux2-vae_small.safetensors\n\n本次仅提供协议入口与连接说明，没有修改本地提示词工具、模型配置或配套工作流。云端保留既有官方工作流。\n\n## 模型选择与目录接口\n\n准备单元提供“全部”（默认）、“仅 ANIMA”、“仅 MOSS”三个启动模型组；只影响本次要校验和恢复到本地的资产，不删除其他已缓存的模型。完整模型集11个权重共39,546,103,000字节（约39.55GB）。\n\nGET /_moss/models 返回 protocol_version=1 和 models 数组。每项含稳定 id、display_name、family、version、checkpoint、text_encoder、vae、assets、suggested_defaults、ready、selected_for_startup。资产路径相对于模型目录；填写 Comfy 节点输入时按 object_info 中的枚举文件名匹配。ready表示所有依赖在本地是普通文件且大小符合清单；完整SHA-256在准备阶段验证，不在每次目录请求时重复计算。\n\n当前稳定 ID：\n\n- moss_image_sft_int8\n- anima_turbo_v1_1\n- anima_aesthetic_v1_1\n- anima_base_v1\n- wai_anima_v1_0\n- animayume_v1_5_base\n- miaomiao_harem_anima_v1_6\n\n建议另一台电脑的出图界面先选家族（MOSS/ANIMA），再选具体模型；选项从云端目录获取，仅ready的模型可提交。MOSS与ANIMA使用不同的编码器、VAE和工作流，不能只替换主模型。suggested_defaults是起始建议；切换模型可提示采用建议值，已经手动修改的尺寸和参数应保留。所有模型共用一个API地址和密钥。\n\nWAI和MiaoMiao使用固定版本的公开镜像下载；文件大小及完整SHA-256已对照作者发布的Civitai元数据。AnimaYume和官方ANIMA来自作者仓库。具体来源、版本和校验值保存在ComfyUI_Colab/model_registry.json。不会自动替换为2.9B Beta，也没有改动本地程序或用户配套工作流。\n\n永久存储提示：Google个人账户免费云盘通常15GB，与Gmail和相册共享；这套模型约40GB不属于免费范围。取消付费存储前需迁移/减少权重，或另行选择从公开仓库下载到Colab临时磁盘的方案。\n"
CLOUDFLARED_SPEC = {'size_bytes':40227721,'sha256':'053b80b0a23031a038fdbf3c073f59f82b8f1f152aa67971d7383ffafc0dbab0'}
CLOUDFLARED_VERSION = '2026.10.3'
GATEWAY_URL = 'http://127.0.0.1:8190'



def gateway_reusable(process, source_digest, upstream_runtime_id):
    return (process is not None and process.poll() is None
            and getattr(process, '_moss_source_digest', None) == source_digest
            and getattr(process, '_moss_upstream_runtime_id', None) == upstream_runtime_id)


def gateway_ready(key):
    request = urllib.request.Request(GATEWAY_URL+'/_moss/info',headers={'Authorization':'Bearer '+key})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(request,timeout=3) as response:
            info = json.load(response)
            return (info.get('service') == 'moss-comfyui-gateway'
                    and info.get('runtime_id') == runtime_identity(globals().get('MOSS_PROCESS')))
    except (OSError,ValueError,RuntimeError): return False


def prepare_gateway():
    global MOSS_GATEWAY_PROCESS, MOSS_API_KEY, MOSS_BROWSER_SESSION, MOSS_GATEWAY_DIGEST
    if not globals().get('MOSS_READY',False) or not server_ready():
        raise RuntimeError('ComfyUI 尚未就绪，请先完成前面的单元格。')
    runtime_id = runtime_identity(globals().get('MOSS_PROCESS'))
    api_dir = DRIVE_ROOT/'api'
    api_dir.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
    (api_dir/'CLOUD_API.md').write_text(API_README,encoding='utf-8')
    (api_dir/'gateway.py').write_text(GATEWAY_SOURCE,encoding='utf-8')
    source_path = Path('/content/moss_gateway.py')
    digest = hashlib.sha256(GATEWAY_SOURCE.encode()).hexdigest()
    process = globals().get('MOSS_GATEWAY_PROCESS')
    if process is not None and process.poll() is None:
        if not gateway_reusable(process, digest, runtime_id):
            process.terminate(); process.wait(timeout=10)
        elif gateway_ready(globals().get('MOSS_API_KEY','')):
            return
        else:
            raise RuntimeError('本笔记本的接口进程未就绪，请查看 /content/moss_gateway.log。')
    with socket.socket() as sock:
        sock.settimeout(1)
        if sock.connect_ex(('127.0.0.1',8190)) == 0:
            raise RuntimeError('8190 已被其他进程占用，未修改该进程。')
    source_path.write_text(GATEWAY_SOURCE,encoding='utf-8')
    MOSS_API_KEY = globals().get('MOSS_API_KEY') or secrets.token_urlsafe(32)
    MOSS_BROWSER_SESSION = globals().get('MOSS_BROWSER_SESSION') or secrets.token_urlsafe(32)
    environment = os.environ.copy()
    environment.update(MOSS_API_KEY=MOSS_API_KEY,MOSS_BROWSER_SESSION=MOSS_BROWSER_SESSION,
                       MOSS_MODEL_CATALOG=str(DRIVE_ROOT/'model_registry.json'),MOSS_MODEL_ROOT=str(LOCAL_MODELS),
                       MOSS_RUNTIME_ID=runtime_id)
    with Path('/content/moss_gateway.log').open('w',encoding='utf-8') as log:
        MOSS_GATEWAY_PROCESS = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable,str(source_path),'--port','8190','--upstream',BASE_URL],env=environment,stdout=log,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,start_new_session=True)
    MOSS_GATEWAY_PROCESS._moss_source_digest = digest
    MOSS_GATEWAY_PROCESS._moss_upstream_runtime_id = runtime_id
    MOSS_GATEWAY_DIGEST = digest
    deadline = time.monotonic()+30
    while not gateway_ready(MOSS_API_KEY):
        if MOSS_GATEWAY_PROCESS.poll() is not None or time.monotonic()>deadline:
            raise RuntimeError('认证接口启动失败，请查看 /content/moss_gateway.log。')
        time.sleep(.5)


def prepare_cloudflared():
    binary = Path('/content/moss_cloudflared')
    saved = DRIVE_ROOT/'project'/('cloudflared-'+CLOUDFLARED_VERSION+'-linux-amd64')
    if not verified(binary,CLOUDFLARED_SPEC):
        if verified(saved,CLOUDFLARED_SPEC):
            copy_verified(saved,binary,CLOUDFLARED_SPEC)
        else:
            part = binary.with_name(binary.name+'.part')
            urllib.request.urlretrieve('https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflared/releases/download/'+CLOUDFLARED_VERSION+'/cloudflared-linux-amd64',part)
            if not verified(part,CLOUDFLARED_SPEC): raise RuntimeError('Cloudflare 官方程序校验失败。')
            os.replace(part,binary); mark_verified(binary,CLOUDFLARED_SPEC)
    if not verified(saved,CLOUDFLARED_SPEC): copy_verified(binary,saved,CLOUDFLARED_SPEC)
    binary.chmod(0o700)
    return binary


def start_cloud_api():
    global MOSS_TUNNEL_PROCESS, MOSS_API_URL
    prepare_gateway()
    process = globals().get('MOSS_TUNNEL_PROCESS')
    if process is None or process.poll() is not None:
        binary = prepare_cloudflared()
        log_path = Path('/content/moss_tunnel.log')
        with log_path.open('w',encoding='utf-8') as log:
            MOSS_TUNNEL_PROCESS = subprocess.Popen([str(binary),'--no-autoupdate','tunnel','--url',GATEWAY_URL,'--protocol','http2'],stdout=log,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,start_new_session=True)
        MOSS_API_URL = None
    # A live tunnel may acquire its URL after a previous attempt timed out.
    log_path = Path('/content/moss_tunnel.log')
    deadline = time.monotonic()+90
    MOSS_API_URL = globals().get('MOSS_API_URL')
    while not MOSS_API_URL:
        if MOSS_TUNNEL_PROCESS.poll() is not None or time.monotonic()>deadline:
            raise RuntimeError('公网连接创建失败，请查看 /content/moss_tunnel.log 后重试。认证接口仍仅在本机监听。')
        log_text = log_path.read_text(errors='replace') if log_path.is_file() else ''
        found = re.search(r'https://[a-z0-9-]+\.trycloudflare\.com',log_text)
        if found: MOSS_API_URL = found.group(0)
        else: time.sleep(.5)
    # The gateway must be reachable through the tunnel before reporting success.
    deadline, last_error = time.monotonic()+60, None
    while True:
        try:
            request = urllib.request.Request(MOSS_API_URL+'/_moss/info',headers={'Authorization':'Bearer '+MOSS_API_KEY})
            with urllib.request.urlopen(request,timeout=10) as response:
                info = json.load(response)
                if (info.get('service') != 'moss-comfyui-gateway'
                        or info.get('runtime_id') != runtime_identity(globals().get('MOSS_PROCESS'))):
                    raise ValueError('Unexpected gateway runtime identity')
            break
        except (OSError,ValueError) as error:
            last_error = error
            if time.monotonic()>deadline: raise RuntimeError('公网接口尚未连通，请重试最后一个单元格。') from last_error
            time.sleep(2)
    connection = {'protocol':'comfyui-http','base_url':MOSS_API_URL,'api_key':MOSS_API_KEY,'auth_header':'Authorization','auth_scheme':'Bearer','scope':'current-colab-runtime','model_catalog':'/_moss/models','runtime_id':runtime_identity(globals().get('MOSS_PROCESS'))}
    # This private runtime file is not copied to Drive. Download it from Colab only when needed.
    Path('/content/moss_connection.json').write_text(json.dumps(connection,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
    display(Markdown('### 云端 API 已就绪\n\n**API 地址：** '+MOSS_API_URL+'\n\n网页入口：[打开 ComfyUI]('+MOSS_API_URL+'/_moss/login)，登录时输入下面的密钥。客户端请求头使用 `Authorization: Bearer <密钥>`。'))
    display(HTML('<label>本次访问密钥（点击输入框后可复制）： <input type="password" readonly autocomplete="off" style="width:420px" value="'+html.escape(MOSS_API_KEY,quote=True)+'"><button type="button" onclick="var f=this.previousElementSibling; f.type=f.type===&quot;password&quot;?&quot;text&quot;:&quot;password&quot;">显示/隐藏</button></label>'))
    print('连接配置位于 Colab 临时文件 /content/moss_connection.json。运行时回收后地址和密钥失效。')
    print('模型目录：'+MOSS_API_URL+'/_moss/models（需要相同的访问密钥）')
    print('接口文档：我的云端硬盘 / ComfyUI_Colab / api / CLOUD_API.md')


start_cloud_api()
